==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* High damage.
* One of the best [[swords]] for grinding and PvP in [[Second Sea]] due to good damage and a long range move.
* Good for any playstyle because of its stuns.
* Good [[sword]] for [[Guns|Gun]] mains because the player can force people into the tick damage of some guns.
* Fun for combos.
** Both gun and sword stats are good for this sword.

|'''[Z] Continuous Slashing'''
* Long stun.
* Decent knockback which counters the endlag.
* Great for teamers.
* Good combo starter.

|'''[X] Dragon Gust'''
* Good for combos.
* Decent range.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Dashes on the fourth click.
* Bad for PvP compared to [[Third Sea]] [[swords]].
* Outclassed by meta swords like [[Cursed Dual Katana]].
* Difficult to combo with.

|'''[Z] Continuous Slashing'''
* Short range.
* The knockback makes it hard to combo with afterwards.
* Can be countered by [[Cyborg (race)|Cyborg race]] or tick damage that can disturb the user who is holding the move.
* Medium endlag.

|'''[X] Dragon Gust'''
* Does not [[break Instinct]].
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Oroshi, along with [[Shizu]] and [[Saishi]] are required (and with 300 mastery on each respectively) to obtain the [[True Triple Katana]]. 
* Oroshi's pre-rework [X] move ('''Scatter Shot''') was much similar to that of pre-rework [[Bisento]]'s.
* Oroshi is often used in skilled builds, together with [[Bizarre Revolver]] and [[Lightning]].
* {{Ability|Z}} is similar to both [[Spin]]'s and [[Dark Blade]]'s [Z] moves, although it is smaller and lasts longer.
** {{Ability|Z}} had a larger hitbox before it was reworked.
